     {
      "type": "mainHeadline",
      "text": "Essentials of Paris",
      "variant": "HEADING_XL",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_title",
      "isBold": true
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>16. June 2025 | 2 min read | Lufthansa Editorial Team</b>",
      "size": "SMALL",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_info"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>A city without stop signs and with a penchant for macarons: five things about Paris that will surprise you.</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_description_0"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_separator"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Rule of Thumb: Right of Way</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_0"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Paris is a bustling metropolis and tourist mecca with world-famous&nbsp;crowded streets and busy intersections such as Place Charles de Gaulle with the Arc de Triomphe at its center. So it’s incredibly hard to believe that Paris doesn’t have a single&nbsp;stop sign on its streets. Not one, none, nada.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_1"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/essentials-of-paris/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par1/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris/lh_app_paris_illustration1_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Illustration on the left: intertwined intersections that wrap around the Arc de Triomphe; right: an oversized baguette on a forklift"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>A City with Taste</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_2"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Its famous cuisine is one of the many great things that Paris is loved for around the world. No wonder it is home to the second-largest wholesale food market on the planet. The Rungis International Market has been trading since the 10th century.&nbsp;Roughly two million tons of meat, vegetables, fish, and cheese are sold there each year.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_3"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
