     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/essentials-of-paris/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par3/separator_copy_copy__1678749679"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Tomato Juice? With Vodka!</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_4"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "The first Bloody Mary is said to have been prepared at the Ritz Hotel in Paris. Rumor has it that this popular cocktail was created for the famous writer Ernest Hemingway. He asked for a drink that didn’t smell like alcohol. As a result, he was served tomato juice with vodka.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_5"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/essentials-of-paris/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par5/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris/lh_app_paris_illustration2_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Illustration on the left: a hand writing with pen and ink on a sheet of paper; right: Catherine de' Medici with a box of macarons in her hand"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>A Pastry with a Journey</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_6"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Since the French patisserie Ladurée opened its stores around the globe, the macaron has become an icon of French cuisine. But get this – the macaron isn’t French! It is of Arabic origin and found its way to Italy before being introduced to the French royal family by Catherine de' Medici in the 16th century.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_7"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Hand Painted</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_8"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "The Eiffel&nbsp;Tower&nbsp;dominates the Parisian skyline like no other building in the city. To keep the 300-meter-high structure in good shape, it has to be repainted every seven years – by hand! This involves the use of 60 tons of paint.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_9"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/essentials-of-paris/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par9/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris/lh_app_paris_illustration3_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Illustration of a person painting the Eiffel Tower"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "All illustrations © Sylvia Neuner",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-paris_paragraph_10"
     }
